  "canonColorDataLayoutsDescription": "Where Canon's ColorData (tag 0x4001; in CR2 in the maker notes, in CR3 in the CTMD track) holds the levels, keyed by version|length: the word of the first of four per-channel black levels; NormalWhiteLevel and SpecularWhiteLevel follow, the latter five words after the first black word. Used for every Canon without its own entry in levelOverrides, only for raw data with a colour filter array (not sRAW/mRAW). LibRaw 0.22.2 uses a higher white level for almost all of these (mostly 16383); Canon's SpecularWhiteLevel is what Adobe's DNG carries for most of them. Found by matching Adobe's and LibRaw's levels across 96 files of 40 models on 2026-09-27.",
  "colorCalibrationDefault": {
